course: dictionary
lesson: 12892
title: Words for uniforms
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You do not need to know every word to understand a text. When you meet a new word, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «The admiral wore a dark blue coat with gold epaulettes on his shoulders.» A dark blue coat, an admiral and gold all point to the shoulders of a smart uniform, so an epaulette must be a decoration there.
explain: Ask yourself what word would fit. An epaulette is a decoration on the shoulder of a uniform, often with gold fringe or stripes that show a person's rank, which is how high they are in a team such as the navy. Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word: «gold decorations on his shoulders» still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: Sometimes an epaulette is just a strap on the shoulder of a coat or shirt, worn for style. «She wore a white shirt with epaulettes on each shoulder.» The clue is the word style, so this meaning fits too. When context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: An epaulette is a noun: one epaulette, two epaulettes.
fact: «Epaulette» means a decoration on the shoulder of a uniform, often with gold fringe or stripes showing rank.
fact: «Epaulette» can also mean a strap on the shoulder of a coat or shirt, used for style.
fact: In US spelling it is written «epaulet», with one t at the end.
fact: Useful phrases are «gold epaulettes» and «shoulder epaulettes».
exercise: «The drummers in the marching band had gold epaulettes on their shoulders.» What is an epaulette? | A kind of drum | A type of hat | *A decoration on the shoulder of a uniform | A small pocket on a bag
exercise: «The captain's epaulettes showed he was in charge of the ship.» What do the epaulettes show? | How old he is | What he had for lunch | *His rank | How far he has walked
exercise: Ruby reads that the US spelling is «epaulet». Which word is the same word spelt the US way? | epaulot | epolet | *epaulet | epaulete
test: «She wore a white shirt with a strap on each shoulder, just for style.» What is that strap called? | A scarf | A necklace | A belt | *An epaulette
test: «The soldiers marched past with shining epaulettes.» What does this tell you about the soldiers? | They were fast asleep | *They wore smart, important uniforms | They were lost in the woods | They were very hungry
exam: In the phrase «gold epaulettes», what does gold tell you? | The coat is wet through | The uniform is very old | It is a kind of food | *The decoration is gold-coloured
